In conclusion, while "here be dragons" has become a symbol of medieval cartography, it is uncertain whether medieval cartographers regularly wrote this phrase on their maps. Further research and analysis of authentic medieval maps may provide more insight into the use of this phrase during that time period. The phrase serves as a fascinating reminder of the blend of myth and reality in historical exploration, reflecting the fears and imaginations of those who ventured into the unknown.
