```

This example usage demonstrates the functionality of the `decimal_to_octal` function by providing sample input values and showing their corresponding octal outputs. By calling `decimal_to_octal(109)`, the function converts the positive decimal number 109 into its octal representation, resulting in "147". Similarly, when calling `decimal_to_octal(-109)`, the function converts the negative decimal number -109 into its octal format, resulting in "-155". 

